PART 4 -- VERDICTS
  [FAIL] V1 the BTFR scatter correlates with the quality proxies (>= 2 proxy families with |rho| >= 0.15, p < 0.05 AND LOOCV R^2 >= 0.10)
         measured: 2 proxies with |rho|>=0.15 p<0.05: ['errV', 'Q'] (families ['a rot', 'd M/L']); multivariate LOOCV R^2 = 0.030 (bar 0.10)
         reading : the systematic-dominated claim judged: the univariate channel DOES see the quality axes (errV rho=+0.21 p<0.01, Q rho=+0.20 p<0.01: galaxies with worse rotation errors / worse quality flags scatter MORE) but the registered multivariate bar fails -- LOOCV R^2 ~ 0.03, the proxy->scatter relation does not generalize in an OLS.  And the dominant systematics are not in SPARC's photometric proxies at all: the M/L-systematic lens (rms 0.189 dex in M_b = 0.047 dex in v) is a MAJOR fraction of the residual sd -- the IMF/M-L convention choice alone moves every galaxy; its amplitude is invisible to e_L/L and fstar because the errors are POPULATION-model systematics, not photometric errors.  Honest scope: the proxies available in SPARC cannot carry the dominant systematics; the direct evidence for the systematic-dominated claim sits in the errV/Q channel and the M/L-lens amplitude.
  [FAIL] V2 the intrinsic upper bound < 5% in v (E1_loocv <= 0.0212 dex)
         measured: E1_loocv = 0.0836 dex = 21.2% (bar 0.0212 dex = 5%); E1(in-sample) = 0.0713 dex; E2 = 0.0144 dex^2
         reading : honest number: intrinsic scatter upper bound = 21.2% (0.0836 dex) -- above the RAR within-galaxy white-noise analogue 0.045-0.052 dex (G036 floor 0.0447, G044 extended 0.0524); the errV-only floor is 0.0219 dex
  [FAIL] V3 the forecast: sigma(BTFR) at M_acc = 0.05 dex (JWST-resolved masses) <= half the SPARC-era observed scatter
         measured: sigma_v(0.05) = 0.0846 dex (21.50%) vs 0.5*sigma_obs = 0.0515 dex (12.60%)
         reading : forecast statement: sigma_v = sqrt(intr^2 + (M_acc/4)^2) with intr = E1_loocv; at the resolved-IMF frontier (M_acc ~ 0.03-0.06 dex) the scatter must shrink toward the errV floor and the intrinsic bound -- a quantitative, falsifiable JWST-era prediction; self-consistency: with the SPARC-era effective M_acc = 0.24 dex the model reproduces the observed rms 26.8%

